---
import CallToAction from "../../components/CallToAction.astro";
import AmbientVideo from "../../components/AmbientVideo.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import PublicLayout from "../../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
---

<PublicLayout title="Product" description="Explore Pulsyr's agent-native backlog, dependency graph, project-scoped MCP tokens, Threads, incidents, and management workspace.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Product" title="A backlog designed for work done by people and agents." lead="Pulsyr keeps project state structured, permissioned, and visible. The web interface remains human-friendly while MCP gives coding agents a deliberate way to read and update the same system.">
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-dark" data-analytics-event="cta_docs" href="/docs/primeros-pasos/">Run it yourself</a><a class="button button-outline" href="/integraciones/mcp/">Explore MCP</a></div>
  </PageHero>
  <AmbientVideo
    src="/media/pulsyr-signal.mp4"
    poster="/media/pulsyr-signal-poster.webp"
    label="Animated Pulsyr signal showing structured project activity"
    fallback="Open the Pulsyr project signal video"
  />
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="card pink"><span class="kicker">Core</span><h2>Lifecycle-aware backlog</h2><p>Items move through validated states from idea to done. Closing requires a reason, and every mutation leaves an event trail.</p></article>
      <article class="card teal"><span class="kicker">Graph</span><h2>Dependencies that compute</h2><p>Typed relationships—blocks, requires, conflicts, related, and part of—turn blocking into derived state instead of another checkbox.</p></article>
      <article class="card lavender"><span class="kicker">Access</span><h2>Project-scoped agent tokens</h2><p>Read and write scopes are explicit. A token is bound to one project, so context and actions cannot drift into another workspace.</p></article>
      <article class="card peach"><span class="kicker">Discovery</span><h2>Priority and search</h2><p>Filter by lifecycle, area, priority, and effort. Optional AI enrichment can estimate impact and surface quick wins.</p></article>
      <article class="card ochre"><span class="kicker">Planning</span><h2>Threads and management</h2><p>Move large ideas through investigation and specification, then track documents, pendings, and a three-level Gantt plan.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><span class="kicker">Operations</span><h2>Incidents and webhooks</h2><p>Bring Sentry issues into a triage container and close work from signed GitHub webhook events linked to a commit.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container comparison" aria-labelledby="control-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Human control stays visible</p><h2 id="control-heading">Automation without a black box.</h2></div>
    <div class="control-grid">
      <article><b>Validated transitions</b><p>The lifecycle rejects illegal moves instead of silently accepting inconsistent state.</p></article>
      <article><b>Role-aware UI</b><p>Owners, members, viewers, and superadmins see only the controls their role permits.</p></article>
      <article><b>Optional AI</b><p>Without external AI keys, the core backlog continues to work and features degrade gracefully.</p></article>
      <article><b>Self-hosted data</b><p>You choose the server, database, integrations, retention, network, and upgrade schedule.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CallToAction title="Use the product and the protocol together." body="Start with the Docker image, then connect one project token to your MCP-compatible agent." />
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .card h2 { margin:1.8rem 0 .8rem; font-size:1.65rem; }
  .comparison { display:grid; grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.15fr; gap:clamp(2rem,8vw,7rem); }
  .control-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1.5rem 2rem; }
  .control-grid article { padding-top:1rem; border-top:2px solid var(--line); }
  .control-grid b { color:var(--ink); }
  .control-grid p { color:var(--muted); }
  @media(max-width:800px){ .comparison,.control-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
